softened:
Whisper naught of life nor love;
Softened winds that seem a breath,
Perfumed, bring no fear of death.

soften:
The Muse I pulled my heart out from my breast
To soften, had herself a sort of heart,
And loved my mortal? He, at least, loved her;

softer:
Slower now, slower now,
Softer the music sighs;
Look, there are beads on your partner's brow

Made green for wearied eyes;
Much softer than the breast
Of mother-dove clad in a rainbow's dyes.

